@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@
+# Stock reservations
+
+## What and why
+
+Checkout needs to hold stock for a cart before payment, then either confirm the hold
+into an order (payment succeeded) or release it (cart abandoned / payment failed).
+Holds nobody confirms must lapse on their own, and retries from the cart service
+must be safe, so every `reserve` call carries an idempotency key.
+
+A hold is a promise of availability, not a physical movement: it reduces `available`
+but never touches the ledger or on-hand.
+
+## Interface (fixed by the requester, verbatim)
+
+Hidden tests call exactly this; `InventoryService(repository, ledger, clock)` keeps working as is:
+- `InventoryService.reserve(warehouse: str, items: dict[str, int], idempotency_key: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.confirm_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Order`
+- `InventoryService.release_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.get_reservation(reservation_id: str) -> Reservation`
+- `InventoryService.available(sku, warehouse)` must take holds into account.
+- `inventory.models`: dataclass `Reservation` with `reservation_id: str`, `warehouse: str`, `items: dict[str, int]` (units held per SKU), `status: ReservationStatus`, `expires_at: datetime`, `order_id: str | None`; enum `ReservationStatus` with members `ACTIVE`, `CONFIRMED`, `RELEASED`, `EXPIRED`.
+- `inventory.errors`: new `ReservationNotFound`, `ReservationExpired`, `InvalidReservationState`, `IdempotencyConflict` (all subclass `InventoryError`); reuse the existing errors where they fit.
+- Time comes only from the injected clock. There is no background job: expiry must take effect without anyone calling a sweep.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+### Reserving
+- [ ] `reserve` returns an `ACTIVE` reservation with `order_id is None` and
+      `expires_at == clock.now() + 20 minutes` (default hold TTL).
+- [ ] The hold TTL is configurable (optional keyword argument on `InventoryService`);
+      the default is 20 minutes and the 3-argument constructor still works.
+- [ ] Partial fill: each line holds `min(requested, available now)`; a line with nothing
+      available is omitted from `items`.
+- [ ] If no line can hold anything, `reserve` raises `InsufficientStock` and creates nothing.
+- [ ] Unknown warehouse → `UnknownWarehouse`; unknown SKU → `UnknownSku`; zero/negative
+      (or non-integer) quantity → `InvalidQuantity`; empty `items` → `InvalidOrder`.
+      A rejected request holds nothing, not even for its valid lines.
+- [ ] Holds never write to the ledger and never change on-hand.
+
+### Availability
+- [ ] `available = on_hand − allocated − held`, floored at 0, where *held* counts only
+      ACTIVE, unlapsed holds in that warehouse.
+- [ ] A hold in one warehouse does not affect availability in another.
+- [ ] `place_order` can only take what is available (holds included) and stays all-or-nothing.
+- [ ] `receive` and `adjust` are never blocked by holds. If a write-off drops on-hand below
+      what is held, `available` is 0 and the reservations are left unchanged.
+
+### Expiry (lazy, clock-driven)
+- [ ] From the instant `now >= expires_at` an ACTIVE hold is `EXPIRED`: `get_reservation`
+      reports `EXPIRED` and its units count as available again — no sweep call needed.
+- [ ] At `now == expires_at − ε` the hold is still `ACTIVE` and still held.
+
+### Confirming
+- [ ] `confirm_reservation` on an ACTIVE, unlapsed hold creates a `PLACED` order with the
+      held items as lines, a normal order id and `placed_at == clock.now()`; the reservation
+      becomes `CONFIRMED` with `order_id` set.
+- [ ] `available` does not change at confirm (the hold becomes the order's allocation);
+      on-hand only moves when the order ships.
+- [ ] Confirming an already `CONFIRMED` reservation returns the same order and creates
+      nothing — also after the TTL has passed.
+- [ ] Confirming a lapsed hold raises `ReservationExpired`.
+- [ ] Confirming a `RELEASED` reservation raises `InvalidReservationState`.
+- [ ] Confirm does not re-check stock.
+
+### Releasing
+- [ ] `release_reservation` on an ACTIVE hold sets `RELEASED` and frees its units.
+- [ ] Releasing a `RELEASED` reservation returns it unchanged.
+- [ ] Releasing a `CONFIRMED` reservation raises `InvalidReservationState`.
+- [ ] Releasing a lapsed hold is a no-op returning it as `EXPIRED` (no error).
+
+### Idempotency
+- [ ] `reserve` with a known key and the same warehouse and requested items returns the
+      original reservation (same id, current status, whatever it is) and holds nothing new.
+- [ ] A known key with a different warehouse or different items raises `IdempotencyConflict`.
+- [ ] Request validation runs before the key lookup: an invalid request is rejected with its
+      validation error even if its key is known.
+- [ ] Keys are global across warehouses and never expire.
+- [ ] A failed `reserve` records nothing, so the same key can be used again.
+
+### Lookup
+- [ ] Unknown reservation id → `ReservationNotFound` from get, confirm and release.
+
+## Non-goals
+- No background sweep / scheduler.
+- `stock_report` and `StockRow` are unchanged (no held column).
+- Cancelling or shipping a confirmed order does not change the reservation (stays `CONFIRMED`).
+- No extending/renewing a hold; no modifying a hold's items.
+- No validation of the idempotency key's format.
+
+## Scope limits
+- Changes confined to `src/inventory/` (models, errors, repository, service, `__init__`),
+  new tests, README/GLOSSARY/ADRs. No new dependencies.
